module_docs.default_argument_handling:
When a function parameter has a default value, the decorator validates the argument only if a value other than the default is supplied. If the default is ``None`` the decorator treats ``None`` as a sentinel that bypasses validation, allowing optional arguments that may be omitted.

Example:
```python
@quantity_input(mass='kg')
